On V4 you're probably best off looking back through the boot
listing.  Uerf is still the simplest way:

# uerf -R -r 300

The "-r 300" is the collection of boot messages.  The -R give them
in reverse chronological order.  New SCSI devices can appear after
the system has booted, so a cross check with scu(8) may also be
useful.  "scu show edt" will show all the devices the subsystem
is currently aware of.  For details of each device you can use
"show device" by name, or set the nexus information by address:

# scu -f /dev/rrz9c show device

# scu
scu> set nexus bus # target # lun #
scu> show device

