Greetings--

On our 4.0D system I believe the longest spindown timeout you can set
is 60 minutes.  Under /etc/sysconfigtab you should find an entry like
the below one, or you can add it to the end of the file.

---- begin excerpt
pwrmgr:
        disk_dwell_time = 60
---- end excerpt

For our group even 60 minutes was an inconvenience.  I solved this
problem with a cron job that runs every half-hour during work hours,
and 'touch'es various file systems.  With this infrequent but
continuous access, the drives stay spinning.  At night the job doesn't
run so they spin down, so the only delay is the first person in the
morning.

Good luck,
Craig


