Starting in V5.0, gethostbyname and gethostbyaddr became thread safe
by default.  As a result h_errno handling became thread safe as well.
The global h_errno was left behind, but we can not guarantee it's
acuracy.

To get the thread value you need a prototype and to use the 
_Get_h_errno() function, like this:

	extern int _Get_h_errno();

	main () {
		gethostbyname(host);
		if (_Get_h_errno() > 0)
			herror();
	}

To set h_error, applications should use _Set_h_errno(error) with the
following prototype:

	extern int _Set_h_errno();
 
Using _Get_h_errno() returns 0 as expected.

Joe


