In article <91tqep$pcv$1@nnrp1.deja.com>, cappelc@my-deja.com writes:

>What is the max dimension of ufs file system?
>And advanced file system?

Supported limits are usually documented in the Release Notes
or Software Product Description, both of which are included
with distributions.

From the V4.0G Release Notes:

UFS supported maximum size:   128 GB
AdvFS supported maximum size: 512 GB

UFS architectural max. size:    1 TB
AdvFS architectural max. size: 16 TB

From the V5.1 SPD:

Nothing said about UFS limits, but they're probably the same.

Nothing is said about a maximum domain size for AdvFS, but
it does have limits for volume and file/fileset size:

Maximum volume size:           1 TB - 512 KB
Maximum File and Fileset size: 1 TB - 512 KB
Voumes in a domain:            256

If you have other limits in mind, you need to be more specific.


