The hardware inventory at boot is shown by the "old" command

	uerf -Rr 300 | more

Also another trick that Solaris can't do

	file /dev/rdisk/*c
or pre V5.x
	file /dev/rrz*c

Note the above command(s) also return the number of error logged against
the particular disk since boot time (something I have yet to figure out
how to do in Solaris).


Jack Patteeuw


