We had the same problem a while back..  Everything was ok, then after a
reboot we couldn't ftp or telnet to the box (even from itself!).
Compaq support wasn't much help at all.   No configuration had changed,
and inetd was running..

After hours of scratching our heads, we went and look into the cluster
inetd.conf file   (of which there are several)  (look
for /etc/inetd.conf.local   which is a link to the cluster/etc one)..
Missing were the lines that help inetd fire off telnetd and ftpd..  If
yours is now blank, add these 2 lines:

telnet  stream  tcp     NoWait  root    /usr/sbin/telnetd       telnetd
ftp     stream  tcp     NoWait  root    /usr/sbin/ftpd          ftpd

I can only IMAGINE why they went blank all of a sudden (especially
after we've been using the box for months)..  My only guess is that the
cluster local files got reset or something..

Has anyone else experienced this?



Richard



