The printcap option ct=tcp is supported as of V4.0a.

Some Xerox printers do not provide tcp/ip socket printing, only lpd
remote
printing.

Testing the printer socket connection using telnet:

        telnet PSPACE04 2501

If the printer provides bi-directional PostScript communication you can
have the printer send back data. PostScript example:
        %!
        (this is a test) print flush

Socket PostScript printing test

  ((cat /etc/motd | /usr/lbin/ln03rof); sleep 5;) | telnet pspace04 2501

This tests converts the motd file to PostScript and sends it to the
printer.
Make sure the printer is up and ready to print, not in power saver mode.

Try changing the print filter from hplaserof to ps_level1of. The
ps_level1of
filter will convert text files to PostScript.



