Use :-

/sbin/sysconfig -q inet

to see the inet subsystem which includes the parameter udp_ttl

Use :-

/sbin/sysconfig -m inet

to see if the subsystem is static or dynamic (i.e - can parameters be
changed dynamically, without rebooting).

Modifying parameters in the inet subsystem requires a reboot. No kernel
rebuild is necessary.

To make the change to the parameter, you can manually
edit /etc/sysconfigtab and include an entry, but the recommended method
is to use the sysconfigdb utility. See the man page for sysconfigdb.

Hope this helps.

Paul.


