Has anyone experience problems using the GNUPro Toolkit that comes with
the freeware CD for osf5.1?

We have experienced major problems an difficulties..

The first being that it doesn't come with GDB (nor will GDB come close
to compiling on the machine).  The version of DBX tends to be
unreliable using the supplied GCC version, and LADEBUG core dumps
consistently.

The second being that without defining  _LIBC_POLLUTION_H_, the header
files that come with GNUPro collide with the system header files (most
notibly, unistd.h..  cuserid redefined)

