As far as I know, the headers that come with DEC C++ have a bunch of
pragmas that will instruct the compiler not to instantiate some of the
commonly used templates. Check if you are using "cxx" to line or
"ld" to link, in the later case, you do not link with libcxxstd.so. That
would
then explain the error that your are getting. You can also recompile your
entire application with __FORCE_INSTANTIATIONS to force the
exclusion of the pragmas.

