Hello Alex,

  it's possible that the compiler can't instantiate the template because
it doesn't find the implementation file for it. Try adding
'-I/usr/include/cxx -I/usr/include' before all other '-I' statements and
try again after a good clean. This *should not* be the problem, but who
knows ? Furthermore, could you indicate which version of cxx you're using
? Templates instantiation is very different from versions 5.x to 6.x.

  Can you also apply /bin/nm on all the object files you're linking with
(either .so or .o) in order to find references to the symbol you're
missing ? (it should look like "/bin/nm file.o | grep 'std::basic_string'"
or something like that) This will allow knowing which file requires the
symbol (it will be flagged as 'U' meaning undefined in the nm output).

  Cheers,

    Jeremie.

