>The answer is 67108864 -- what do I do with this number to get megabytes
>or gigabytes?

In the world of UNIX:
1KB = 1024 bytes
1MB = 1024 KB
1GB = 1024 MB
To those who are not computer-technically inclined:
1Kb = 1000 bytes
1Mb = 1000 Kb
1Gb = 1000 Mb

So when you know the # of bytes, divide by 1024 the proper number of times 
to find M or G, depending on what you want.



