Hey TMan,

It's easy, sorta like riding a bicycle, as long as you already know
how!  If you understand the concepts of disks, subdisks, plexes, and
volumes, you're halfway there.

The LSM manual for the V5 stream deleted the appendix full of examples
which was part of the V4 manual, so you might want to grab the latter.
Things get much easier once you've seen examples.  See Appendix C of the
following:

http://tru64unix.compaq.com/faqs/publications/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V40D_HTML/AQ3NCETE/TITLE.HTM

There are 2 ways to control LSM: top-down ("gimme some storage and I
don't care where it comes from") and bottom-up ("I know what disks and
partitions on specific controllers I want to use and I am going to tell
you how to use them").  I recommend the latter method in the strongest
possible terms.

Below is a shell script I used to set up some LSM stripes; maybe it'll
help you get started.  I'll check back on this thread next week to see
if you still need help.

WJD

list="24 30 36 42 54 60 66 72 90 96 102 108 25 31 37 43 55 61 67 73 91
97 103 109 26 32 56 62 27 33 39 45 57 63 69 75 93 99 105 111 28 34 40 46
