> ...keep tapping ctrl-C until a SRM prompt appears.

That's what I usually do if the "auto_action" console environment
variable is set to BOOT and the jumper is set to reset.

> If all else fails, disconnect power to the boot device.  That's SURE to
> get you the SRM or AlphaBIOS... 

Yeah, I never thought of this one.  Thanks for the tip.

> SRM is a miniature OS in the firmware, and it is used in place of the
> BIOS in a PC.  

We call it the "console" (a poor choice of terms, IMHO).  The SRM is the
System Reference Manual - a document which, among many other things,
specifies the APIs that allows the console to commumicate with the OS.

